{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1463592-werewolf-heart-of-the-forest-just-played-it-twice-and-it-was-fantastic","id":1463592,"title":"Werewolf: Heart of the Forest - just played it twice and it was fantastic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-12T08:05:32-07:00","id":1463592,"title":"Werewolf: Heart of the Forest - just played it twice and it was fantastic","content":"This is a visual novel based on Werewolf the Apocalypse, with the writer of The Witcher 1 at the helm.<br /> <br /> <b>What it is:</b> a fantastic, atmospheric, and beautifully written choose-your-own-adventure styled game that allows you to decide how Maia, your character, navigates the complex political and ecological quandary affecting the sole remaining old growth forest in Poland. You can be confrontational and violent, cunning and withdrawn, you can get the police and media on your side or have them be your enemies, you can choose which pack and tribe you end up in, etc. There's a surprising amount of choice, and after two play throughs I can attest to your choices making a difference.<br /> <br /> But the best part is how the game captures the <i>feel</i> of Werewolf. The dreams, the pressure from the spirit world, the visceral connection to the forest, the ambiance. It's a masterclass in writing and atmosphere, and the character voices (written, there's no narrators) are unique and distinctive.<br /> <br /> <b>What it's not:</b> an actual game in the sense of running around killing things. There is violence, there is death, and there can be a lot of it, but you're not playing a traditional game - this is a visual novel, so you have to immerse yourself in the music, the art, and the narrative, and enjoy the tale through the choices you make.<br /> <br /> 10/10. If you enjoy Werewolf, and want an evocative experience that immerses you faithfully in the lore and setting, Werewolf: Heart of the Forest is the way to go.<br /> <br /> You guys played it? What did you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T12:28:36-07:00","id":1463606,"title":"","content":"I enjoyed the game, it was a little short but the very atmospheric and the story was solid. The first change into Crinos was great IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/355-romanov","name":"romanov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar355_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T07:52:02-07:00","id":1463703,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed it and offered it to my players (all new players), it's great maybe a little bit to short to my taste, but that's because it's so well done. As you say it's everything together that make it so good sounds, drawings, ambiance. I'm just missing the philodox run for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"",